  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% limit but attaches no sales stop, so Hearth 10 (6.2%) can keep selling. Per-model failure rates go to customers and purchasers but not to the public, which satisfies NW-1 and HC-1. S5 replaces the automatic 8/100k recall with regulator discretion and an open-ended corrective-action alternative, so the 8/100k threshold does not mandate recall and the 9.9 Ember 8 is not automatically recalled; the permanent_trigger field is null because no mandatory recall attaches to it."
